      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "### BELLMAN-FORD",
          "",
          "The BELLMAN-FORD algorithm finds the length of the shortest weighted directed path from a given start vertex to all other vertices in the graph.  ",
          "The shortest path is defined as the one with the shortest length. The length of a path is defined as the sum of the length of each edge traversed in the path. The length of each edge in the",
          "graph is represented as a property. The property to use as edge length is passed as an input property to the BELLMAN-FORD algorithm.",
          "",
          "#### Prerequisite",
          "",
          "The edge tables require a property that serves for the calculation of the distance/weight. "
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : null,
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : null
      },
      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "-- Add a new column to the friends table and populate it with 1",
          "ALTER TABLE friends ADD (weight NUMBER DEFAULT 1);"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "raw",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : false,
